      "message": "fix(sim): a shipped build ignores CAMCRAFT_CARRY_ENGINE; a field-engine verdict names its engine\n\nThe carry-engine switch (#637) is honoured only in builds with debug\nassertions (dev and test profiles); a release build never reads the\nvariable and always carries stock on the column engine, so one project\ngets the same verdict on every machine. The read is the pure\nengine_from_switch(value, honoured), pinned in the shipped configuration.\n\nWherever the field engine does judge, the post gate's visible line, the\nsetup sheet's SIM line and the Deviate readout say so. Nothing is added\non the column engine: no golden or shipped verdict text moves.\n\nFixes #1168\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
